# Identity and Access Management (IAM)
### Identity
it can be <br>
- dev team
- an applicaiton
- azure vm
- azure service
- service 

### Access
what are the things you are allowed to do <br>
example, user1 can access SQL database but cannot access Cosmos DB


### authentication
who are you. <br>
login + Multi Factor Authentication (MFA)


### Authorization
what can you do <br>
you can read the data, write the data, delete the data. <br>
can be user / application / VM also

### Identify
who / what is requested <br>
it can be person or service
resources can be VM or storage or databse

To control all these we have Microsoft Entra ID. <br>
Previously this serviec called as Microsoft Active Directory

# what Microsoft Entra ID contains
in Microsoft Entra ID we have
- users
- groups
- applications
- service principle principles
- managed identities
- devices

### this access managemnt can be done at 4 levels
> when we work with RBAC (Resource Based Access Control)
> We can give access on different scopes

1. this means we can give access at  management group level. mgmt group means we have multiple azure accounts group
2. you can give access on a `subscription` level also, means divide billing based on subscription
3. give permission on `resource group` level also. it is logical grouping of resources. all resources will be managed at RG level permission.
4. we can give permission on resource level, meast on VM or SQL serer.

> Note: try to give least privileges to user. it means give only requried access to users
